<title>JAPAN: Sakura Bank falls on cross-shareholding cuts.</title>
<headline>Sakura Bank falls on cross-shareholding cuts.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sakura Bank Ltd shares retreated on Wednesday morning for the ninth consecutive session, depressed by dissolving of cross share-holdings, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0153 GMT, the shares were down 22 yen at 760, with trade totalling 3.24 million shares. It was the second most heavily traded issue on the first section of the Tokyo bourse.</p>
